Hello,

Anyone running 7.2 on a UDB/Multia?  Just curious about any upgrade 
problems or success stories, and how stable it is running.

I'm currently running 7.0 with updated kernels and everything runs well 
except for a lockup problem when I update the time in crontab hourly -- 
the kernel stops functioning normally (it doesn't crash, just stops 
working well). There's a few posts about this problem in the archive, but 
I was never able to find a working solution. Since the clock on the multia 
drifts a lot, it becomes a pain to manually synch it up every few days.

Anyone updating both the system clock and hardware clock through crontab 
on a Multia? What kernel and redhat release are you running?

	-Jeff







