I've been putting off upgrading my Multia from 6.2 to 7.2 as there are
sure to be issues doing the install. As far as I remember (my memory will be
worse than usual, just got home from work and it's 12:30am) 7.2 can
only be installed via SRM and the Multia SRM has a bug which means you can't
install using it - somewhat of a chicken and egg problem. You could compile
a kernel that will boot via AlphaBIOS but it'll be a bit fiddly - may be easier
to do from a 7.0 install, more problematic for me starting at 6.2.

It may be possible that the newer MILOs can boot a 7.2 kernel - can someone
confirm/deny this? Jay do you wish to add something to this rambling missive?

Off to bed me thinks.


