To the list:

I have seen similar postings before and should have saved them!  I installed RH 7.2 in my PWS500a/u, using the server setup and adding a number of packages including the video drivers for 3dLabs, TGA, S3V and SVGA.  I have a batch of Permedia and Glint video cards but am using the Oxygen VX1 32 meg PCI card.

The install goes well (I've done this twice now), including the Xserver setup, real good resolution in either the KDE or Gnome screen and at any setting I pick.  When I boot, though, the screen goes black as it usually does just before the login screen comes up.  What should happen next is a brief replay of the video bios message and th login screen.

What actually happens is .... nothing.  No combination of key will bring the screen back to life, although a Ctrl-Alt-Del will usually shut down the machine fairly cleanly.

i remember reading similar cases where the screen output was being sent to the serial port.  I don't have any way of testing if this is the case (at least I don't think i do), and I can not remewmber if anyone has posted a remedy for this problem.

The machine worked great under RH 7.1, and is running Tru64 clean and solid. Could there be something wrong with my choice of installed packages? What next?

jn

AKA "Thursday"

--bound1033660004--




