On Thursday 03 October 2002 4:46 pm, Jon Norstog wrote:
> What actually happens is .... nothing.  No combination of key will bring
> the screen back to life, although a Ctrl-Alt-Del will usually shut down the
> machine fairly cleanly.

Does Ctrl-Alt-Backspace not kill X and return you to a command line login?
Failing that, Ctrl-Alt-F1-5 should also do the trick and give you a command 
prompt. From there do (as root) a `telinit 3' to get back to pre-X mode.

Another suggestion would be to go into the interactive startup, not start X, 
login at the console and then run startx to see what happens (or run 
XConfigurator if that doesn't work).

cheers
john




