I read in a Mozilla mailing list that Sun has made the standard
edition 1.4.0 SDK source available, after registering and
agreeing to a license and so forth.  However, the related web
pages (accessed from
http://wwws.sun.com/software/java2/download.html) indicate you
have to have access to a binary 1.4.0 SDK in order to build and
install from source.  For some strange reason, :-) Sun's site
does not show a listing for Alpha Linux.  So, without a binary,
we would seem to be stuck.  Is there a known solution to this
chicken-and-egg problem?

On a related topic, does anyone on the list know how to get gcj
to work?  I have Java 1.3.1 from Compaq IIRC, but gcj says it
cannot find the java.lang package.  Is there a magic environment
variable or -classpath switch needed that isn't obvious from the
man pages and such?

Also, is there a way to get Java to work with Mozilla 1.1 on
Alpha?

Thanks.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net




