This morning I came into my office to find my Alphastation 250 4/266
spewing register save messages on the screen.  After some spewage, it
attempts a reset sequence

00, 01....

but does not get very far before it spews some error messages which I
can't read before the register save messages scroll them off the screen.

So I tried a cure-all fix:  power off and back on.  Now it does nothing
at all; no messages on the screen, no boot attempt, nothing.  The
graphics card is a ZLXp-E1; a simple frame buffer.  The POST LEDs seem
to settle on FC, indicating the ARC console initialized.  But the LEDs
keep cycling through some tests and keep coming back to FC.  I thought
I was always using SRM.

I have so far removed all SCSI devices, tried removing all the RAM, but
none of that changed anything.  I will next remove the graphics card
and try to hook up a serial terminal to the console port.

