Hi,

after having installed rh72 quite successfully on a couple of
Ruffians, I tried an AS200 today. Milo is from Stefan@suse, like the
one my Ruffian really liked.

So I got mili-2.2.18-avanti, put it and linload.exe (and ldmilo.exe
for that matter) on a floppy, put cd 1 in the drive, created thje boot
menu entry (tried both ldmilo and linload) and at the milo prompt I
typed

boot sr0:kernels/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/scd initrd=images/cdrom.img

This did it nicely on Ruffian, but on AS200 (Avanti/Mustang) the
kernel gets loaded and started, but complains that it cannot see the
root device "scd".

Any ideas?

I know NOTING about srm, but if anyone could post the equivalent line
to start installation from cdrom, I'd be happy to try. The machine is
"100% original".

Thanks,
Ingo





