On Fri, Oct 04, 2002 at 10:32:49PM -0500, Bharat Raghunathan wrote:
> 
> I have installed Redhat 7.2 on an Alphastation AS200 4/166
> machine. Console/etc seems to work, though I cannot get X setup
> successfully.
> 
> The machine has a TGA card, and the monitor I am using is a HP4033A
> monitor. Is this a workable combination, and if so, what do I have
> to do to get it to work successfully.

If that HP monitor is a fixed frequency one, then chances are you won't
be able to get it to work, unless you're very lucky.

If it's a multi-sync, you should be fine; the TGA server will do the
right thing if you fill in the monitor specs (horizontal and vertical
refresh rates) correctly in the XF86Config-4 file.

You will need to put in a "BusID" option line in the Device Section
of the config file; find the TGA's PCI slot position via "lspci"
(eg something like "00:0a.0 DEC TGA graphics 21030" would be turned
into:

	BusID	"PCI:0:10:0"	/* note hex to decimal conversion */

Good luck.

 --Jay++

