On Fri, Oct 04, 2002 at 09:52:05PM +0200, Ingo T. Storm wrote:
> 
> 128MB. Should be enough for an install and a future firewall - no X
> requiered here. I'd think it#s not the amount of RAM here, but a MILO
> limitation regarding the size of ramdisks.

Yes, 128MB is fine for those purposes.

I think you're right about it being a MILO problem. The latest MILO I
used was able to handle the "cdrom.img" part of the install with no
problem, but earlier ones may be more problematic. Are you sure you
have the latest?

> >I think you may need to use the floppy install technique,
> 
> ouch. The docs are a bit sparse in this respect. Maybe someone from
> the srm camp can fill me in on a simple cdrom boot? I know how to get
> to an srm prompt (and back;-).

There are "generic.img" and "ramdisk.img" in the images/ directory on
CD #1. Put them on floppies via "dd". Boot the "generic" one via:

	>>> boot dva0 -fi vmlinux.gz -fl 1	# 1 == text mode install

and be ready to insert the "ramdisk" one when the kernel asks for it.
Proceed then as usual.

Good luck.

 --Jay++

