This is not Alpha specific but Red Hat Linux specific. I'm hoping 
someone in the list knows a solution.

We ran into a problem in the lab when students tried to change their 
passwords. When someone issued 'passwd' command, all others 'passwd' 
commands hung (No prompt back). This situation can be recreated easily 
with just 2 users.

I know it needs the locking on the file to be written, but should it lock during the dialog. Some user might need more time to decide his/her new password after types 'passwd' command. Things get worse in a class room environment. It seems nobody can change their password. 

Is this standard, or is it configurable? Does anyone know a solution for this problem?

FYI - I find out that SUSE Linux' passwd does not have this problem.

-- 
AC






