> Date: Tue, 08 Oct 2002 21:16:38 -0400
>
> I noticed that RH8.0 has build an open-office RPM.
>
> does gcc have a 32 bit address compile and link option?
>
> Just a silly thought but this may be a way around the problems of no 
> open office. Since all the ugly part of open office building is handled 
> in the RPM.

At least on RH7.1 (and its ancestors), there is a -taso option
that handles most things to sidestep non-64-bit-clean code.
The other thing that is sometimes needed is the personality()
system call.  IIRC, I used PER_LINUX_32BIT to build Squeak on
RH6.1 or 7.0 many nearly two years ago.  (Squeak is the _MOST_
non-64-bit-clean program in existence.  Every object reference
in the Smalltalk object space is stuffed into 32 bits.)

Good luck.

Robert Riches
