Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"; format=flowed

With regards to your message at 09:58 AM 10/14/02, Pedro AF. Cunha. Where 
you stated:

>Hello,
>I ve an Alphaserver 800 5/400 and I m trying to install, from SRM, the Red 
>Hat 7.2.
>After doing all the needed selections, the installation continues copying 
>packages and then freezes randomly. It seems to me to be a SCSI problem, 
>because after freezing starts doing some SCSI resets.

It would appear you may have a SCSI error problem.
For installation you might try disconnecting any devices not strictly 
needed (temporarily) and then installing. It is also a good idea to have an 
active terminator on the end of the SCSI bus, rather than passive or 
termination by a drive device.

>This is the list of the Hardware:
