Where you stated:



Hello,
I ve an Alphaserver 800 5/400 and I m trying to install, from SRM, the
Red Hat 7.2.
After doing all the needed selections, the installation continues
copying packages and then freezes randomly. It seems to me to be a SCSI
problem, because after freezing starts doing some SCSI resets.

It would appear you may have a SCSI error problem.
For installation you might try disconnecting any devices not strictly
needed (temporarily) and then installing. It is also a good idea to have
an active terminator on the end of the SCSI bus, rather than passive or
termination by a drive device.



This is the list of the Hardware:

2 x NCR 53c810 (External storage atached)
Can you temporarily disconnect these fro installation? Then if/when you
successfully installit re-connect them?



