On Tuesday 15 October 2002 14:08, Uncle George wrote:
> George France wrote:
> >
> > Alignment traps are not a serious bug but will make the code run
> > significantly slower.  They are mostly really annoying.
>
> Your opinion is amusing.  If the kernel didnt bother fixing these faults,
> then you'd have a dead program - but some incentive to fix the problem. If
> the kernel could fix them, then you pay the price in delayed execution of
> that faulty instruction - with fairly no incentive to go and get it fixed.
> If the processor is so fast, then maybe its not even worth bothering.
> So what would it take for this fault to escalate into a serious matter.  On
> a 266Mhz 21064 machine, it may warrent an evaluation. on a 800mhz 21264,
> under the same condidions it may warrent a yawn.  And a different type of
> person may change that concept alltogether.
>

It is precisely because the kernel fixes the faults that it is not a serious
problem. It is just question of whether or not you can live with the delay.

Best Regards,


--George




