> This brings to mind a question.
>
> Are unaligned accesses guarenteed to generate an error or the correct
> results. Although the correct results may require some huge amount of
> processing on the part of the kernel to repair the problem.

On the Alpha Architecture, unaligned accesses are guarenteed to generate
an error.  The error is trapped by the kernel and fixed by the kernel.  The
kernel will always make the correct fix for alignment at cost of cpu cycles.

Beest Regards,


--George




