After trying many things suggested by many helpful folks, I finally
gave up and re-installed the RH 7.2 on my UP2000+.  This last time, I
did a custom install, and manually selected groups of components,
including the kernel development options.  After the install, I was
pleasantly surprised to see the kernel source already installed, along
with a few other things I was installing manually.

Now the bottom line:  I connected my old disk from the Tru64 system,
and lo and behold, it recognized the UFS partitions.  I was able to
mount and save all the files that I needed there.  I did not need to
build a custom kernel.  However, the system did not recognize any of
the AdvFs partitions, and I did not see any support for it in the file
system part of xconfig.  So I'm guessing that data may be lost, unless
I can find another Tru64 system to mount it on.

So again, thanks to everyone on their attempts to help me.  The efforts
are greatly appreciated.

eyc




