Your converted code makes sense.  A prettier method is used by the 
kernel in asm/unaligned.h via:

              get_unaligned(ptr);
              put_unaligned(val, ptr);

More information can be found at:  

   http://www.xml.com/ldd/chapter/book/ch10.html

under the section titled "Data Alignment".

>
> I spent a lot of time tracking this one down and could only come to the
> conclusion that the unaligned trap handler was not working correctly.

If I had to take a wild guess, then I think that the unaligned trap handler
is working correctly and that it is more likely that you have found a compiler
optimization bug, which would explain your difficulty in reproducing the
problem.  Have you tried rebuilding your application with -O1, '-O2 
-fno-sched-interblock' or '-O2 -fno-strength-reduce'???

> I was hoping to come up with a nice small proveable case but I just
> could not seem to make things break on demand. and the only other way to
> get this to break would involve kicking 40 customers off line(Not to
> likely).

I hope this helps.

Best Regards,


--George




