  Hello everyone.

  Sorry for the off-topic, I just wonder if there's a switch for g77 to make a
double precision number out of real fp number (not defined, used by default).
The piece of code

	a=1.
        b=a+1./1e12
        c=b-a
        write(*,*) c
        end

compiled with g77 cuts off everything after 8 digits left of point. Since
what's left are 8 zeros, the result is 0.
  I got the (almost) right result using Compaq fort with -real_size 64, but
don't know that there's something equivalent in g77.

  Thank you in advance,


