Hello Eugene and all.

Yesterday I had a chance to use ES45(4 proc.) in HP Japan for
testing SMP with Super Page.
For this test I made a quick patch for RedHat 7.2/Alpha.
(It does not support vm_align option nor i386/sparc64)

It worked fine at least for my test. IIRC, I did:

1) make a copy of RedHat 7.2 kernel source tree.
2) in the copied directory, copy the RedHat configuration to '.config'
   The configuration file is in the configs directory.
   cp configs/kernel-2.4.9-alpha-smp.config .config
3) patch the kernel. I uploaded the patch file in
         http://shimizu-lab.dt.u-tokai.ac.jp/lsp.html
4) make menuconfig and turn on Super Page Support
5) make dep; make boot modules modules_install
6) mkinitrd initrd-2.4.9-superpage.img 2.4.9-superpage
7) copy kernel and System.map
   cp arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz /boot/vmlinuz-2.4.9-superpage
   cp System.map /boot/System.map-2.4.9-superpage
8) Rewrite /etc/aboot.conf
9) reboot the system

The transw benchmark on my web runs about 3 to 4 times faster on ES45
with superpage.
I ran SPEC benchmarks but it did not finished until I leave HP Japan.
The staff of HP will send me the result of SPEC benchmarks later.

I hope you will enjoy the super page.

Regards,
-- 
