The error is being issued due to a change in binutils.
>From what I gather that linker error check was placed in
intentionally.  See:

http://sources.redhat.com/ml/libc-hacker/2002-06/msg00022.html
http://sources.redhat.com/ml/libc-hacker/2002-06/msg00023.html

The first message has a patch for glibc or you can try a newer
glibc rpm.  I built redhat's glibc-2.2.93-5 this past weekend
and it seems to have the fix.

I'm not sure how to fix Mozilla.  I have not checked to see
if a bug relating to this has been filed yet.  I doubt it as
it will not compile using gcc 3.x without patches.  That's a
known bug, see

http://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=86446

And even if you get it to compile, plugins will break until you
recompile those to pick up the gcc 3.x C++ ABI changes.

Alan

