> 
> 	You could always set boot_osflags to a non-existant entry and
> 	aboot will stall and ask you what you want.
> 	
> 	SET BOOT_OSFLAGS 7
> 
> 	Unless you have 7 entries, it should stall.

Instead of relying on such dirty tricks it is better, if you
are using aboot, to set boot_osflags to 'i' which is defined as
a flag which makes aboot to go into an interactive mode.  Otherwise
what you will do if all 10 labels are already used?

But I guess that the original question is how to get to SRM
prompt while autobooting (hitting repeateadly on ctrl-C usually
works).  Then one can type 'b -fl i' and this will work too.

  Michal




