If you can't get the SRM prompt via normal means, how about
temporarily modifying /boot/etc/aboot.conf so no listed option
will work?  That should get you to at least the aboot prompt,
from which a little luck will get you to the SRM prompt.  Another
idea (mentioned via email) might be to unplug the disk to get the
regular boot to fail and get you to the prompt.

