Hello,
we are currently moving a Rawhide machine to Linux. We encountered two
problems:

a) Only UP 2.4.18 boots. SMP kernels crash early in the boot. This
   crash has already been reported on the Linux kernel list but the
   reporter has not received any answer:

http://marc.theaimsgroup.com/?l=3Dlinux-kernel&m=3D102148667732098&w=3D2

   Is it possible to get SMP running on the rawhide ?


b) TGA2. I know these beast are problematic. We tried some XFree 4.2
   but only got a shifted, very low resolution display (at most
   640x480). Currently we got an old Mach64 which we try to get to
   run.

   This board is not an Powerstorm. It is rather small, it has a white
   IBM chip on it, an Bt485 RAMDAC and a CirrusLogic chip. Is it
   possible to get this to some sensible resolution like 1024x786 ?

Thanks for any pointers/suggestions

