On Fri, Oct 25, 2002 at 08:46:50AM -0400, Benton, Marco wrote:
>
> actually, the TGA2 *is* a PowerStorm.  DEC called it a PowerStorm 3D30 or
> something like that.  there were 2 of them, 1 with 8-bit color depth at
> 1280x1024 and the other card can do 24-bit color at 1280x1024 (or higher).

Yes, 8-plane TGA2 was called PowerStorm 3D30, and the 24-plane TGA2
was the PowerStorm 4D20, IIRC.

> the TGA is supported but not the TGA2.
>
> this should shed some light: http://www.xfree86.org/current/DECtga1.html

Not so.

The doc is out of date - TGA2 is actually supported in XFree86 4.1.0 and
later, just that none have gotten around to fixing it.

The "BusID" option must be specified for TGA2 as well as TGA, and the
driver name is still just "tga" for both flavors.

