On Sat, Oct 26, 2002 at 08:29:38AM -0700, Robert M. Riches Jr. wrote:
> While running up2date on RH7.1 Alpha, I got the following error
> messages:
> 
> rpmdb: Suspiciously high nelem of 4294967295 on page 0
> error: db4 error(-30979) from db->verify: DB_VERIFY_BAD: Database verification failed
> 
> Is the message spurious?

Probably not.  Something is not nice in your database.

> If not, what is the correct remedial action?

Try 'rpm --rebuilddb' and hopefuly this should correct things. Takes a
while.  Make sure that there are none of lingering rpm processes holding
locks to your database before trying that.  If this will fail (most
likely it will not) then go on search through archives of rpm mailing
list (on Google, for example).

This is absolutely CPU type independent. :-)
 
   Michal




