Hello,
my CPU fan is starting to make strange noises, so I tried replacing
it. I bought a PC fan with identical size. It is 12V and 0.17 A
(instead of 0.21A as currently installed). I rewired it as described
in an earlier set and installed it. But the system is now extremly
unstable. Booting from disk usually jumps back to SRM during hard disk
mounting/checking; on subsequent tries not even a kernel is loaded,
just a cycle and back to SRM. Booting from jumpstart goes a little
farther, but as soon as the disk are accessed, I am back to SRM.
Installing the old fan "cures" the problem. Now the system is stable
again.

What do I have to check to get a proper fan ? The manual of Samsung
explains in great detail how to attache and detach the fan but is
silent on the issue of specifications.

Thanks,

                  Helge
